    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5ce3efbc-8685-3e54-bf88-444b9798bf7f",
                "word": "bipennated",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2755a94b-012b-3731-a42a-49cee37c11fc",
                        "entry_id": "5ce3efbc-8685-3e54-bf88-444b9798bf7f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having two wings."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "527b2f1a-0f7b-4aab-bf6a-c82bb905cab3",
                                "sense_id": "2755a94b-012b-3731-a42a-49cee37c11fc",
                                "text": "bipennated insects"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d77ee66-9096-45ff-a7d2-60bbeed86de4",
                                "sense_id": "2755a94b-012b-3731-a42a-49cee37c11fc",
                                "text": "For the keeping the Body steady and upright in Flight, it gernally holds true, (if I mistake not,) that all bipennated Infects have Poises joined to the Body, under the hinder Part of their Wings; but such as have four Wings, or Wings with Elytra, none."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e54588ba-7334-451a-ac67-92ee826dfdd7",
                                "sense_id": "2755a94b-012b-3731-a42a-49cee37c11fc",
                                "text": "Those that like cocks on dunghills fight without any serious provocation, only want a pair of fine glossy wings and red hat crests to be classed among the bipennated bipeds of the air ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "22a3515f-1ff5-4214-a33d-01de3eadb71a",
                                "sense_id": "2755a94b-012b-3731-a42a-49cee37c11fc",
                                "text": "Smash cupid, the bipennated buooooy, the little farceur, whilst he is yet a child' somther him before he has time to become a tremendous Titan in the plenitude of his power to do for you; smother him, oh! some-other him, and live to see how jolly miserable your light of other days will make some other man!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a33dc5fd-cabd-30ec-8e7b-080fe7d692b3",
                        "entry_id": "5ce3efbc-8685-3e54-bf88-444b9798bf7f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having two shafts, blades, petals, or extensions from a single central point or body."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "edec8966-2751-4d0e-b289-6ce68bdf4373",
                                "sense_id": "a33dc5fd-cabd-30ec-8e7b-080fe7d692b3",
                                "text": "Very branching, branches bipennated, and very close, nearly imbricated ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf80ac7b-df0a-4511-8371-e97fb70822a6",
                                "sense_id": "a33dc5fd-cabd-30ec-8e7b-080fe7d692b3",
                                "text": "Each auricula was bipennated with a single meatus externus, so that this development was not strictly preternatural; the lambs possessing, in fact, two ears only."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f55cc83-d2d6-4e13-b3d8-1957c4eabde4",
                                "sense_id": "a33dc5fd-cabd-30ec-8e7b-080fe7d692b3",
                                "text": "Some other birds have bipennated feathers—black-game and grouse, for instance; and I well remember that during the visit of one of my nieces a discussion arose upon the question of such feathers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3de68e2-a724-42f9-a873-f6af547759ce",
                                "sense_id": "a33dc5fd-cabd-30ec-8e7b-080fe7d692b3",
                                "text": "M. palmaris longus (figs. 13, 15, 29) is a bipennated muscle arising by tendon fibers from the medio-distal part of the medial epicondyle of the humerus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a2ea11d-4b9b-4675-8d08-ac43e44fdd9a",
                                "sense_id": "a33dc5fd-cabd-30ec-8e7b-080fe7d692b3",
                                "text": "Bipennated leaves with small leaflets;"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
